<body>
<h1>Retro Formats — Selection Card</h1>
<h2>mad-sad-glad</h2>
<p>Fastest to run. Use when team is fresh + in-person + retro is the first or second of the cycle. Skip when distribution is async (low-signal anonymous responses).</p>
<h2>4ls (Liked, Learned, Lacked, Longed For)</h2>
<p>Use mid-cycle when the team wants more reflective categories than mad-sad-glad. Good after launches; balances positive + critical.</p>
<h2>sailboat (anchors / wind / rocks / island)</h2>
<p>Visual metaphor; use when team needs to surface blockers + aspirations. Strong on hybrid; can do anonymous-async on a digital whiteboard.</p>
<h2>lean-coffee</h2>
<p>Use when topic-list is unknown — team votes the agenda. Best with stable in-person teams. Skip when shy contributors get bulldozed.</p>
<h2>anonymous-async</h2>
<p>MANDATORY for distributed async teams (UA/PT/UK timezones, P4 outsource). Submit cards anonymously via form/board; facilitator clusters; live discussion happens at recap. Skip only if team is fully co-located.</p>
<h2>Selection rule (one-liner)</h2>
<pre><code>distribution == async              → anonymous-async
fatigue == fatigued                → rotate to a format not used in the last 2 retros
fatigue == fresh + in-person       → mad-sad-glad
mid-cycle + reflective need        → 4ls
visual metaphor + blockers focus   → sailboat
agenda is unknown                  → lean-coffee</code></pre>
</body></html>
